# openOODA x86 Backend Final Audit — 2026-08-25, post-fix snapshot

Logline: One-shot final audit of the x86 backend state after the 5-shape refuse gate, the per-arm wrote counter, the silent fall-through fix, the SSA per-block remap fix, and the Float SIMD fix have all landed; summarises pre-fix vs post-fix numbers, names the remaining work, and gives a verdict and the next 3 actions.

Setup: Reads ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo (209 lines, the post-fix dispatcher with four gates wired in at lines 49-91), openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot (67 lines, the post-fix floor snapshot), audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot (167 lines, pre-fix ground truth on 6,936 fixtures), audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot (159 lines, SSA static projection), and audit/x86-5shape-refuse-post-fix.oot (110 lines, 5-shape gate static audit). No compiler run. No file edits. No /tmp writes.

Beats:
  1. Recap the pre-fix numbers from the v2 hostile probe and the SSA static projection.
  2. Project the post-fix numbers for every tracked metric.
  3. List the remaining work that keeps the backend from PASS.
  4. State the final verdict with one line of reasoning.
  5. State the next 3 actions ranked by impact.

File: openOODA/audit/x86-final.oot
Status: smoke — read-only final audit, 2026-08-25
Scope: x86 backend only; AArch64 status lives in openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot §3

---

## 1. Pre-fix vs post-fix numbers

Pre-fix ground truth: audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot (6,936-fixture probe, 5,750 COMPILED on emit-x86, 508 on emit-x86-ssa). Post-fix projection: audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot (central estimates from static analysis of the four landed fixes). All percentages are of the listed base.

| # | Metric | Pre-fix | Post-fix | Change |
|---|--------|---------|----------|--------|
| 1 | emit-x86 COMPILED | 5,750 / 6,936 (82.9%) | 5,750 / 6,936 (82.9%) | unchanged (gate refuses, does not compile) |
| 2 | emit-x86 REFUSED | 1,185 / 6,936 (17.1%) | ~3,800 / 6,936 (~55%) | +2,615 (5-shape gate + per-arm wrote counter convert silent miscompile to clean REFUSED) |
| 3 | emit-x86 ASM-FAIL | 1 / 6,936 (0.0%) | 1 / 6,936 (0.0%) | unchanged (the lone multi-main case stays) |
| 4 | Silent miscompile (empty stdout, of COMPILED) | 2,607 / 5,750 (45.3%) | ~580 / 5,750 (~10%, central 0.4%, range 0.4-7.4%) | -2,027 to -2,595 (-35 to -45 pp) |
| 5 | Of which no-op main (push/sub/add/syscall) | 2,595 / 2,607 (99.5%) | ~0 (5-shape + wrote counter refuses) | -2,595 (the dominant class is gone) |
| 6 | SSA ASM-FAIL | 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) | 0-147 / 6,936 (0.0-2.1%, central 0.0%) | -6,279 to -6,426 (-90.5 to -92.6 pp) |
| 7 | SSA COMPILED | 508 / 6,936 (7.3%) | 6,789-6,936 / 6,936 (97.9-100%) | +6,281 to +6,428 (+90.6 to +92.7 pp) |
| 8 | Float empty-stdout (of Float fixtures) | 158 / 160 (98.7%) | ~0 (Float refused at gate, SIMD/FP fold handles the rest) | -158 (-98.7 pp) |
| 9 | 3-arm match empty-stdout (of 3-arm fixtures) | 27 / 30 (90.0%) | ~0 (3-arm refused at gate) | -27 (-90.0 pp) |
| 10 | Result[T] empty-stdout (of Result fixtures) | 179 / 216 (82.8%) | ~0 (Result refused at gate, real path is tagged-union 3-arm) | -179 (-82.8 pp) |
| 11 | struct field/type empty-stdout | 224 / 277 (80.8%) | ~0 (struct refused at gate) | -224 (-80.8 pp) |
| 12 | List[T] empty-stdout | 162 / 202 (80.1%) | ~0 (List refused at gate) | -162 (-80.1 pp) |
| 13 | v1 300-sample silent-miscompile rate (reference) | 118 / 300 (39.3%) | n/a (post-fix is on the 6,936 set) | +6.0 pp (sampling artifact, not a regression) |
| 14 | 5-shape gate verification (Sig / RealH / Msg) | n/a (gate did not exist) | 5/5 / 5/5-with-1-note / 5/5 (x86-5shape-refuse-post-fix.oot §1) | new audit lane |
| 15 | Per-arm wrote counter arms | 0 of 6 | 6 of 6 (free, list, match, opt, struct, typed_let) | +6 arms |

**Reading.** Metrics 4, 6, 8-12 are the headline wins. Metric 1 (COMPILED) is unchanged by design — the fix converts silent miscompile into clean REFUSED, not into more compile passes. Metric 2 (REFUSED) is the inverse view of metrics 8-12. Metric 15 is the new structural guarantee: six dedicated arms now refuse on `wrote == 0` rather than emitting a no-op main.

---

## 2. Remaining work (numbered, ranked by impact)

1. **Gate the channel / while / for / parallel no-op main class.** ~221 fixtures affected (channel 35/46 = 76.0%, while 79/105 = 75.2%, for 103/151 = 68.2%, parallel 4/4 = 100%). Not caught by the 5-shape refuse gate (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) and not caught by the per-arm wrote counter (6 arms: free, list, match, opt, struct, typed_let). If left unfixed, the central silent-miscompile estimate of 0.4% drifts toward the upper bound of 7.4%. Source: audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133, audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:104.
2. **Close the 12 residual "real write, wrong string" silent-miscompile class.** 12 binaries produce a real write syscall but the syscall writes the wrong string (the hardcoded `fold-me` / `0` / `1` / `line-a` clusters). Add a post-emit run-time check in the `_start` wrapper that asserts the output buffer contains the expected source-id or prints `<name>: no-output` and exits 1. ~30 lines. Source: audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:98, audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:154.
3. **Port the per-arm wrote counter and the 5-shape refuse gate to aarch64_emit.** Closes the HIGH risk identified in audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot:74 (silent fall-through to 22-arm chain) by making AArch64 fail-closed on the same 5 shapes. Mirrors aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo from x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+ and wires at aarch64_emit.oo:18-26. Source: audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:73, openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot:33.
4. **Fix the LLVM SSA pipeline (mem2reg + dce are unsound).** std/compile/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo (57 lines) maintains a single `cur_val` across every store/load, does not track slot identity, does not insert Phi, does not rename; std/compile/llvm_codegen/ssa_opt.oo (100 lines) `ssa_opt_dce` is an identity transform. CSE is not in the file. P0.3 marks both as residual. Source: openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot:48, SHIPPED.oot:33-36.
5. **Fix the 3 over/under-refusal smells in x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo.** (a) Shape 1 real-handler over-restricts to `println(ident)` only — chain's x86_collect_and_emit_float accepts `println(foldable_expr)` where expr is STAR/PLUS/MINUS/SLASH on let names. (b) Shape 4 real-handler requires KW_TYPE AND DOT but the chain also supports the bare `struct S { ... }` form. (c) Shape 5 real-handler requires `list_len` but the chain's x86_match_list also accepts `list_get` and `list_set`. Source: audit/x86-5shape-refuse-post-fix.oot §2 Issues 1-3.
6. **Resolve the c_emit two-gate rebuild blocker.** Pure multi-module oodac rebuild cannot complete: Gate 1 (host `check` of main.oo) trips on token-count cap; Gate 2 (C compile of stitched all.c) trips on `conflicting types for 'OoL_<Name>'` because c_emit_olist.oo:25 and c_emit_struct.oo:104 both emit a real typedef. The smallest fix is an `OO_HAVE_<Name>` ifndef guard plus a tightened stitcher regex. Source: audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:11-13, 28-42, 74.
7. **Re-run the 6,936-fixture probe to confirm the projection.** ~3 hours wall time. Required to move the SSA ASM-FAIL projection from 3/5 to 5/5 confidence and to measure the actual post-fix silent-miscompile rate on the full set. Out of scope for static projection. Source: audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot §5.
8. **Run a 100-fixture stratified SSA smoke probe** (50 duplicate-label, 50 undefined-block). Confirms the per-block remap fix without the 3-hour cost. Source: audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:148-149.

---

## 3. Final verdict

**PARTIAL.** Three of five critical bugs from openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot §4 are fixed (no-op main for the 5 top hostile shapes, SSA per-block remap, Float empty-stdout). Silent miscompile projects from 45.3% to a central 0.4% (range 0.4-7.4%). SSA ASM-FAIL projects from 92.6% to a central 0.0% (range 0.0-2.1%). The backend is now fail-closed at the gate rather than silent-miscompile-positive. Two real risks remain in the x86 lane (channel/while/for/parallel no-op main class not gated, LLVM SSA pipeline unsound) and one structural risk crosses lanes (the aarch64_emit shim still falls through silently to a 22-arm chain without a refuse gate). The backend is not yet a usable product floor (PASS would require zero residual silent-miscompile classes and a green 5/5-confidence probe), and it is no longer the "not a usable product floor" the v2 probe called it. PARTIAL is the honest label.

---

## 4. Next 3 actions

1. **Add a 4th refuse gate at ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo:85-92** between the wrote counter and the 22-arm chain. The gate scans for `KW_CHANNEL` / `KW_WHILE` / `KW_FOR` / `KW_PARALLEL` and either refuses with a typed-AST escape message or routes to a real emitter. New file: ooda/oodac/x86_emit_4shape_refuse.oo (≤ 256 lines, mirrors the 5-shape gate). Estimated impact: drops the central silent-miscompile estimate from 0.4% toward 0.0%; clears the 221 affected fixtures out of the no-op-main class. Source: audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133, openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot:65.
2. **Port the 5-shape refuse gate to aarch64_emit.** Create ooda/oodac/aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo (≤ 256 lines) as a mirror of x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+ (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]). Wire at aarch64_emit.oo:18-26 between the existing Tier 0 contract / diag / secret gates and the dispatch ladder. Estimated impact: closes the HIGH silent-fall-through risk named in audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot:74; gives AArch64 the same fail-closed posture x86 now has. Source: openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot:33, 66.
3. **Run a 100-fixture stratified SSA smoke probe** to move the SSA projection from 3/5 to 4/5 confidence. Sample: 50 fixtures that previously failed with duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels + 50 that previously failed with undefined `.Lmain_block*` forward references. Execute `oodac --x86-elf-ssa` on each, assert `as` and `ld` both exit 0, and assert the .bin runs in under 2s. If 100/100 pass, the central SSA ASM-FAIL case is confirmed and the §2 Item 7 3-hour full re-run can be deferred to a calmer window. Source: audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:148-149, 152.
